WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:05.819
Module two. Message templates. The pre-approved messages you need before you can

2
00:00:05.819 --> 00:00:07.136
Start a conversation.

3
00:00:09.333 --> 00:00:13.563
On the API, a business cannot simply message anyone with any text.

4
00:00:13.563 --> 00:00:18.370
The first message to a customer must use a template that Meta has approved.

5
00:00:18.370 --> 00:00:23.498
That protects customers from spam, and it protects the Oribrix number from being

6
00:00:23.498 --> 00:00:24.010
Blocked.

7
00:00:24.460 --> 00:00:26.252
First, why templates exist.

8
00:00:26.702 --> 00:00:28.644
Then the three template categories.

9
00:00:29.094 --> 00:00:31.398
Then building a template, field by field.

10
00:00:31.848 --> 00:00:34.130
Then variables, buttons and the preview.

11
00:00:34.580 --> 00:00:37.738
And finally, Meta approval and what each status means.

12
00:00:40.133 --> 00:00:42.862
Every template must be in one of three categories.

13
00:00:42.862 --> 00:00:47.173
Picking the right one matters, because Meta prices and checks them differently.

14
00:00:47.623 --> 00:00:52.588
Utility. Important updates and notifications the customer expects, like order

15
00:00:52.588 --> 00:00:56.199
Confirmed, dispatched or delivered, or payment received.

16
00:00:56.649 --> 00:01:02.003
Marketing. Anything promotional. Offers, new products, a festive sale, or a message

17
00:01:02.003 --> 00:01:04.841
To bring back a customer who has gone quiet.

18
00:01:05.291 --> 00:01:10.880
Authentication. Only for one-time passwords, like a login or verification code.

19
00:01:13.267 --> 00:01:17.542
Don't try to hide an offer inside a utility template to make it cheaper.

20
00:01:17.542 --> 00:01:21.461
Meta checks the content and can move it to the marketing category.

21
00:01:21.461 --> 00:01:26.448
And if a template's category changes in the middle of a campaign, the platform stops

22
00:01:26.448 --> 00:01:30.248
That campaign, so the remaining customers don't get the message.

23
00:02:10.433 --> 00:02:12.289
Here's how to create a new template.

24
00:02:12.739 --> 00:02:17.422
Open Manage, then Template messages. There are ready-made templates for different

25
00:02:17.422 --> 00:02:20.312
Industries, which you can use as a starting point.

26
00:02:20.762 --> 00:02:23.216
Or click New on the top right to make your own.

27
00:02:23.666 --> 00:02:28.733
Choose the category, the language, and a name. The name is only for your reference.

28
00:02:28.733 --> 00:02:32.519
Customers never see it. Use clear names like order dispatched.

29
00:02:32.969 --> 00:02:37.108
Pick the header type: text, image, video, carousel or document.

30
00:02:37.558 --> 00:02:40.694
Write the body, add an optional footer, and add buttons.

31
00:02:41.144 --> 00:02:43.661
Check the preview on the right, then click Submit.

32
00:02:46.067 --> 00:02:47.816
Let's look closer at the fields.

33
00:02:48.266 --> 00:02:52.052
The body text can be up to one thousand and twenty four characters.

34
00:02:52.052 --> 00:02:53.408
Keep it short and clear.

35
00:02:53.858 --> 00:02:58.634
Variables, written as numbers in double curly brackets, are filled for each

36
00:02:58.634 --> 00:03:03.602
Customer. For example, hello, then variable one for the name, your order, then

37
00:03:03.602 --> 00:03:06.914
Variable two for the order I D, has been dispatched.

38
00:03:07.364 --> 00:03:12.131
Sample values. For each variable, give an example value, so Meta's reviewer

39
00:03:12.131 --> 00:03:13.657
Understands the message.

40
00:03:14.107 --> 00:03:18.379
Media. For an image or video header, you don't need the real file now.

41
00:03:18.379 --> 00:03:21.552
You add the actual image when you send the campaign.

42
00:03:22.002 --> 00:03:25.608
Footer. A short line at the bottom, like the Oribrix tagline.

43
00:03:26.058 --> 00:03:30.303
And the language. Many Indian and international languages are available.

44
00:03:32.700 --> 00:03:36.860
Buttons make it easy for customers to respond. There are a few types.

45
00:03:37.310 --> 00:03:41.494
Quick reply. One tap answers, like interested or not interested.

46
00:03:41.494 --> 00:03:46.398
The reply comes back to the live chat, so you know exactly what they chose.

47
00:03:46.848 --> 00:03:52.018
Visit website. A button that opens a link, for example track order, or download the

48
00:03:52.018 --> 00:03:52.267
App.

49
00:03:52.717 --> 00:03:56.919
Call phone. A button that calls a number, like the Oribrix support line.

50
00:03:57.369 --> 00:04:01.593
And a talk to support quick reply, which starts a live chat with an agent.

51
00:04:04.000 --> 00:04:07.968
After you submit, the template appears in the All section with its status.

52
00:04:08.418 --> 00:04:12.557
Pending. Meta is reviewing it. Usually this takes only a few minutes.

53
00:04:13.007 --> 00:04:16.804
Approved. It's ready to use in campaigns and through the API.

54
00:04:17.254 --> 00:04:21.259
Rejected. Read the reason, fix the template, and submit again.

55
00:04:21.259 --> 00:04:26.491
Common reasons are the wrong category, missing sample values, or misleading text.

56
00:04:28.900 --> 00:04:33.636
Here's a starter set of templates that Oribrix customer care would use every day.

57
00:04:34.086 --> 00:04:36.497
Order confirmed, as a utility template.

58
00:04:36.947 --> 00:04:39.379
Order dispatched, with a tracking link button.

59
00:04:39.829 --> 00:04:42.965
Order delivered, with quick reply buttons for feedback.

60
00:04:43.415 --> 00:04:45.825
Payment received, or refund processed.

61
00:04:46.275 --> 00:04:50.478
A marketing template to bring back customers who haven't ordered in a while.

62
00:04:50.928 --> 00:04:55.451
And a talk to support button on most templates, so customers can reach a person.

63
00:04:57.867 --> 00:05:02.398
Quick check. Which category should a, your order has been dispatched, template use?

64
00:05:02.398 --> 00:05:03.435
Think for a moment.

65
00:05:07.385 --> 00:05:12.654
The answer: utility. It's an important update the customer expects, not a promotion.

66
00:05:15.467 --> 00:05:17.174
Let's summarise module two.

67
00:05:17.624 --> 00:05:21.165
The first message to a customer must use an approved template.

68
00:05:21.615 --> 00:05:25.050
The categories are utility, marketing and authentication.

69
00:05:25.500 --> 00:05:30.267
The body is up to one thousand twenty four characters, and variables need sample

70
00:05:30.267 --> 00:05:30.684
Values.

71
00:05:31.134 --> 00:05:34.526
Buttons can be quick replies, website links or a call button.

72
00:05:34.976 --> 00:05:38.048
And a template is pending, approved or rejected.

73
00:05:38.048 --> 00:05:40.288
In module three, we send campaigns.

74
00:05:42.700 --> 00:05:48.417
That's the end of module 2. Next up, module 3: Campaigns and automatic messages.
